What can I say?

118
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:51,070
Well, if you're really curious — I'll be honest, Romanov talked about an oscillating circuit where one half is stable and the other unstable.

119
00:05:51,730 --> 00:05:52,750
Think about that.

120
00:05:53,630 --> 00:05:54,150
And why?

121
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:56,250
What pushes the current?

122
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:57,610
Voltage pushes the current.

123
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:00,030
High voltage from the Kacher.

124
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,350
Our current is insane.

125
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:04,170
Why?

126
00:06:04,310 --> 00:06:08,240
Because there's an insane magnetic field in the coil's inductor.

127
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:11,640
It all looks classic, like Tesla.

128
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,200
Why does Tesla wind it this way?

129
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,520
Inductor at the bottom, the whole coil on top.

130
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:20,400
That is, the coil's stability is here.

131
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,760
Reflected waves come up on top.

132
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,520
A standing wave forms.

133
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,180
It's roughly the same here.

134
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:27,980
Well, something like that.

135
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:31,120
Anyway, here it is, working.

136
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:31,940
The whole rig.

