148
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,840
It's pointless.

149
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:20,920
Nikola Tesla always said: if you want to make a feedback loop powering a system through voltage, your chances are zero.

150
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:32,620
If you want to make self-powering using a magnetic field, your chances equal the very success you're seeing here now.

151
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,400
So, that's the system.

152
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:41,220
It works like that, and essentially there's nothing complicated about it.

153
00:07:41,760 --> 00:08:01,960
The only thing — to use it in industry, so to speak, or to put it into production or anything like that — well, you have to make a proper phase auto-tuning so the

154
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,480
frequencies don't drift, and think about that.

155
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,320
Well, Kapanadze's is more stable, of course.

156
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:12,580
I'm actually thinking right now about building a Kapanadze-type system.

157
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:20,200
