00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:03,820
I hope it's clear to you.

192
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:08,040
Although, basically, a lot of people wind coils trying to squeeze something out of them.

193
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:09,540
Nothing comes out.

194
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,620
Well, naturally.

195
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:17,480
I mean, you have to do a bit of work to understand how the LC circuit works.

196
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:22,240
And basically the coil Akula wound isn't quite right.

197
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:24,460
Now Dolichnaya's coil is a bit better.

198
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:32,680
There you have three separate coils that work the right way.

199
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:34,320
A separate LC circuit.

200
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:42,720
A separate pickup coil that just dumbly goes straight into the diode bridge, no funny business whatsoever.

201
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:45,960
And the inductor, which is a regular induction coil.

202
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,580
Why did Akula use an induction coil?

203
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:51,140
Because an induction coil gives an insane magnetic field.

204
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,960
That's exactly what we need to achieve.

205
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,140
